<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Port of Spain</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Port of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/trinidad">Trinidad</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tobago">Tobago</a>, on the Gulf of Paria in north-western Trinidad. It became the island's capital under Spanish rule in 1757 and grew after British conquest in 1797 into the centre of colonial government and trade. From 1958 to 1962 it was the seat of the federal government of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-indies">West Indies</a> Federation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/port-of-spain.jpg" alt="Port of Spain" width="320" height="217" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DizzyNN · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:POS_at_night_Skyline.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
